       "text": "Three sources, three answers on Monroe County home prices in September.\n\n• Pocono Mountains Association of REALTORS® (MLS closed sales): median sales price $339,500, up 1.3% year over year.\n• Redfin: median sale price $328,764, down 1.9%, measured over a three-month window.\n• Realtor.com's Monroe County market page: a double-digit year-over-year gain.\n\nUp, down and way up, for the same county in the same month.\n\nNone of them is necessarily wrong. They measure different things: different data feeds and coverage, one month versus three, and in some cases listing data alongside sales data. A monthly median also moves a lot on a small sample. PMAR's September median was based on 186 closed sales.\n\nThe standard I hold myself to when a seller or buyer asks about \"the market\":\n1. Use MLS closed-sale data as the source of record.\n2. Say what it doesn't capture. PMAR's median and average sales prices don't account for seller concessions.\n3. Lead with the durable number. Through September, PMAR's year-to-date median was $338,700, up 7.5%.\n\nIf you explain the market to clients, whether as a lender, an attorney or an agent, the most useful thing you can do is name your source and its definition before you say the number.\n\nAlexa Sanchez · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · (570) 688-8147\n\n#PoconoRealEstate #MonroeCounty #HousingData"
