       "text": "Every few months there's a headline about record tourism in the Dominican Republic. And somebody uses it to sell you a condo.\n\nHere's the number. About 9.24 million visitors from January through September, up seven and a half percent from last year. That's real. It's government data.\n\nBut visitors are not your bookings. A record year for the country doesn't tell you how many nights your unit will rent, at what price, or what's left after the management company, the HOA and the cleaning fees.\n\nBefore you buy for rental income, ask for that specific unit's numbers. Actual booked nights. Actual nightly rates. Actual expenses. If all you get is a tourism stat and a gross yield, that's marketing.\n\nThat's not a reason to skip the DR. It's a reason to ask better questions."
