       "text": "How long does it take to sell a house in Monroe County?\n\nIn September 2026, homes that sold in Monroe County spent an average of 58 days on the market before an accepted offer. The year-to-date average through September was 62 days. (Source: Pocono Mountains Association of REALTORS® Monthly Indicators, September 2026.)\n\nTwo things to know:\n• That count stops at the accepted offer. Closing usually takes several more weeks for inspections, appraisal and financing.\n• It's a countywide average. A well-priced home can move faster. An overpriced one can sit much longer and often sells after price cuts.\n\nOther websites may show different \"days on market\" numbers because they measure from different points or use listing data. The figure above is based on actual MLS sales.\n\nPlanning a sale in East Stroudsburg, Stroudsburg or elsewhere in the Poconos? Tap Call for a timeline built around your home.\n\nAlexa Sanchez · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · 528 Seven Bridges Rd, Suite 108, East Stroudsburg, PA 18301"
