       "text": "Closing up your Pocono place for the winter? Do this before you lock the door.\n\nOne. Don't shut the heat off. Keep it on low. Frozen pipes are the expensive version of this video.\n\nTwo. Ask a plumber about shutting off the main water and draining the lines, especially if nobody will be there for weeks.\n\nThree. Put in a temperature and leak sensor that texts your phone. Way cheaper than finding out in March.\n\nFour. Line up someone to plow and someone to check inside. Not drive by. Walk in.\n\nFive. Read the vacancy language in your homeowners policy, or call your insurance agent. Policies can treat an empty house differently.\n\nAnd if you're thinking about selling in the spring, the last thing you want is a winter leak you have to disclose."
