       "text": "ANGLE ID: TT5-N07\nSTATUS: Copy complete · needs footage\nCORE ARGUMENT: PA requires revenue-neutral rates in the first reassessment year, with up to a 10% increase by separate vote. Individual bills shift up or down.\nAUDIENCE: Monroe County homeowners\nTAKEAWAY: It's about your slice, not the size of the pie.\nFORMAT: Talking head, ~45 sec · Effort: Low\nSOURCES:\n• Act 156 of 2016 summary (53 Pa.C.S. §8823) — https://www.legis.state.pa.us/WU01/LI/LGC/BS/2015/0/SB0899P1065.pdf\n• Monroe County: effective January 2028 — https://www.monroecountypa.gov/news/news/2023/countywide-reassessment-a-commitment-to-ongoing-equity\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Overlap check vs GBP1: GBP1 = timeline and what to do; TT5 = how the tax math works."
