       "kind": "text",
       "text": "Monroe County is reassessing every property. The first thing people say is: so my taxes are going way up.\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nThe new values take effect in January 2028. And Pennsylvania has a rule for the year a reassessment kicks in. Every taxing body, the county, your school district, your township or borough, has to reset its rate so it brings in the same total money as the year before. Then, with a separate vote, it can raise that total by up to ten percent.\n\nSo the whole pie can't explode. What changes is your slice.\n\nIf your home's new value went up more than most, your bill can go up. If it went up less than most, your bill can go down.\n\nThe real question isn't whether values go up. It's whether yours went up more than your neighbors'."
