       "text": "As of November 2, every new appraisal report submitted for a loan sold to Fannie Mae or Freddie Mac has to use UAD 3.6, the redesigned Uniform Appraisal Dataset.\n\nWhat's changed:\n• The familiar fixed forms, including the 1004 most of us learned to read, are replaced by a single, dynamic Uniform Residential Appraisal Report built on structured data.\n• On September 30 the GSEs confirmed the November 2 date, with a one-time policy exception process for lenders that couldn't finish implementation in time.\n• FHA has announced its own move to UAD 3.6.\n\nWhat it means on the transaction side:\n1. The report your buyer or seller gets back will look different. Expect questions, and read it before you summarize it.\n2. Transitions create friction. Ask lenders whether their appraisal panel is fully on the new format, and leave a little room in appraisal timelines this quarter.\n3. My read: structured condition and feature data will be easier to compare and to question. That makes a seller's documentation of updates (permits, dates, receipts) more valuable, not less.\n\nAlexa Sanchez · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · (570) 688-8147\n\n#Appraisal #MortgageIndustry #RealEstate"
